{color:#0747a6}*Test Data & Environment Details:*{color}

QA (Microsoft Edge)
OSOS ERP 3.480.1

{color:#0747a6}*Prerequisites:*{color}

# User should have logged to 3.0 application

{color:#0747a6}*Steps to reproduce:*{color}

# Navigate to the screen with the dropdown. (Feature implemented dropdown) 
# Click on the dropdown to activate the search input.
# Try to type a value with a space (e.g., "United Status")

{color:#0747a6}*Actual Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

Pressing the spacebar has no effect; space character is not entered in the search input.

{color:#0747a6}*Expected Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

User should be able to type space characters in the search input to search for multi-word options.



{color:#0747a6}*Attachments*{color}

!image-20250612-032419.png|width=1907,height=1008,alt="image-20250612-032419.png"!

{color:#0747a6}*Test Data & Environment Details:*{color}

QA (Microsoft Edge)
OSOS ERP 3.470.0

{color:#0747a6}*Prerequisites:*{color}

# User should have newly created Tenant from Central hub side

{color:#0747a6}*Steps to reproduce:*{color}

# Try to login newly created tenant
# Enter relevant Credentials for login
# Change the password

{color:#0747a6}*Actual Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}
The system not completing the onboarding and getting errors

{color:#0747a6}*Expected Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

User onboarding process needs to work as previously

{color:#ff5630}*When a user is created from the HRMS → Employee Management module, the telephone number field is not required. However, in the 3.0 system, the telephone number is marked as a mandatory field. Due to this mismatch, if a user created via HRMS (without a telephone number) is later edited in the 3.0 interface, the system throws a validation error preventing the update.*{color}

{color:#0747a6}*Test Data & Environment Details:*{color}

QA (Microsoft Edge)
OSOS ERP 3.483.2

{color:#0747a6}*Prerequisites:*{color}

# User should be logged in to OBP 3.0 system.

{color:#0747a6}*Steps to reproduce:*{color}

# Go to HRMS → Employee Management.
# Create a new user without entering a telephone number.
# Now go to the 3.0 system and try to edit the same user.
# Save the changes without modifying the telephone number.


{color:#0747a6}*Actual Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

Validation error is triggered due to missing telephone number, even though the user was originally created without one via HRMS.

{color:#0747a6}*Expected Result*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color}

User details should be editable without errors, or the system should prompt the user to enter a telephone number before saving from HRMS side.

{color:#0747a6}*Attachments:* {color}

# 
!image-20250613-190507.png|width=1912,height=1011,alt="image-20250613-190507.png"!



# 
!image-20250613-190524.png|width=1853,height=756,alt="image-20250613-190524.png"!

{color:#0747a6}*Suggested Fix:*{color}
Ensure both systems have consistent validation rules or apply conditional logic during update to handle missing fields gracefully.

